    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_77a874665f009226da396f955d3f5c2e40dd0fbae148e6158e3c76ffd904f627",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The span reduces the theorem-closing estimate to a parameter calibration through V: Proposition 2.4 replaces the shifted moment W by V, the two boundary terms become cosine- and sinh-weighted integrals of log V, and the reported choice R=6.8, b=0.64, P(x)=3(x/b)^2-2(x/b)^3 yields N(X,Phi)<=0.79 X S(1;Phi)+o(X). This gains a finite explicit interface between the moment estimate and the final inequality, but the last numerical certification remains an unreplicated source report.",
