    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_42d6780d5a5aac5c671d66ca301de39102ef40695dad291be4b090d310063437",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Square-free reindexing converts the coupled mollifier coefficient sum into products of one-variable convolutions to which a uniform contour lemma applies. Splitting the shared factor gamma at the taper breakpoint then produces two different reductions: the short range is selected by a single surviving contour pole and a multiplicative partial sum, while the long range becomes an integral in Q, Q-prime, and Q-double-prime whose simplification is governed by the taper's endpoint conditions.",
