    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_685b0f1917e76173bbcfaf86e1f51329709f25bd893ccf35eb3100817eead970",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Poisson summation initially separates the zero mode P(l) from all nonzero modes R0(l), but this frequency split is not yet a principal-term/remainder split: square nonzero frequencies produce P2(l), and after the functional equations place P and P2 in the same Euler-gamma representation, their delta-residues cancel exactly, leaving only the tau-residue contributions.",
